# Field type mapping

One row per kind of field. Use it to fill the field spec table, then use the same decision in every
layer (SQL, entity, request, response, mapper, TS interface, form model, form input, tests).

| Kind | SQL | Entity (Java) | Request validation | TS type | Form model / input | List/detail display |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Required short text | `VARCHAR(n) NOT NULL` | `String`, `@Column(nullable = false, length = n)` | `@NotBlank @Size(max = n)` | `string` | `string`, `<input type="text">` | value |
| Optional short text | `VARCHAR(n)` | `String`, `@Column(length = n)` | `@Size(max = n)` (+ `@Pattern` if format) | `string \| null` | `string`, `<input type="text">`, `toRequest`: `model.x \|\| null` | `value ?? '—'` |
| Formatted code (VIN, NIP, postal code) | `VARCHAR(n)` exact length | `String` | `@Pattern(regexp = "...", message = "must be ...")` (+ `@NotBlank` if required) | `string` | `<input type="text">` | value |
| Email | `VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL` | `String` | `@NotBlank @Email @Size(max = 255)` | `string` | `<input type="email">` | value |
| Phone | `VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL` | `String` | `@NotBlank @Pattern(regexp = "\\+?[0-9 -]{6,20}", message = "must contain 6 to 20 digits, spaces or dashes, optionally starting with +") @Size(max = 20)` | `string` | `<input type="tel">` | value |
| Long text | `VARCHAR(1000)` | `String`, `length = 1000` | `@Size(max = 1000)` | `string \| null` | `<textarea>` | value |
| Integer | `INTEGER NOT NULL` | `Integer` | `@NotNull` + `@Min/@Max/@Positive` | `number` | `number \| null`, `<input type="number">`, `toRequest`: `model.x!` | value |
| Decimal / money | `NUMERIC(12, 2) NOT NULL` | `BigDecimal`, `@Column(nullable = false, precision = 12, scale = 2)` | `@NotNull @DecimalMin("0.00") @Digits(integer = 10, fraction = 2)` | `number` | `number \| null`, `<input type="number" step="0.01">` | value |
| Required date | `DATE NOT NULL` | `LocalDate`, `@Column(nullable = false)` | `@NotNull` (+ `@PastOrPresent` / `@FutureOrPresent`) | `string` (ISO) | `string`, `<input type="date">` | value |
| Optional date | `DATE` | `LocalDate` | none (+ rule annotation) | `string \| null` | `string`, `<input type="date">`, `toRequest`: `model.x \|\| null` | `value ?? '—'` |
| Boolean flag | `BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` | `boolean`, `@Column(nullable = false)` | none; record component is primitive `boolean` (missing → `false`) | `boolean` | `boolean`, `<input type="checkbox">` inside the label | `value ? 'Yes' : 'No'` |
| Enum | `VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL` | `@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING) @Column(nullable = false, length = 20)` + separate `enum` file | `@NotNull` | string union | `Type \| ''`, `<select>` with `<option value="">Select {label lowercase}</option>`, `toRequest`: `model.x as Type` | `LABELS[value]` |

## Notes

- Default lengths when the description gives none: names 50 (person names 100), codes = exact
  length, email 255, phone 20, free text 1000.
- Required strings use `@NotBlank`; never `@NotNull` alone for strings. Message comes from Bean
  Validation defaults (`must not be blank`), English thanks to the fixed locale.
- `@Pattern`, `@Email` and `@Size` accept `null`, so optional fields only carry the format rule.
  Remember a blank string `""` sent to a field with `@NotBlank` **and** `@Pattern` produces two errors
  for that field; `@Email` accepts `""`.
- Every custom `@Pattern` gets a human `message` (see `VehicleRequest.vin`).
- A rule that needs code (relative to the current year/date, cross-field) becomes a custom
  constraint annotation + `ConstraintValidator` like `@ProductionYear`, or a service check if it
  depends on other data (then it is a 409, not a 400).
- Uniqueness:
  - case-sensitive (codes, VIN): `existsByX(String)`, `existsByXAndIdNot(String, Long)`;
  - case-insensitive (email, usernames): `existsByXIgnoreCase(String)`,
    `existsByXIgnoreCaseAndIdNot(String, Long)`; store the value as entered.
  - Always also add `CONSTRAINT uq_{table}_{column} UNIQUE ({column})` in SQL.
  - Optional unique fields: only check when the value is not `null`.
- Column naming: snake_case of the field (`plannedHandoverDate` → `planned_handover_date`), aligned
  with spaces in the `CREATE TABLE` like `V1__vehicle.sql`.
- H2 reserved words cannot be table or column names: `user`, `order`, `value`, `values`, `key`,
  `year`, `month`, `day`, `hour`, `minute`, `second`, `limit`, `offset`, `table`, `row`, `group`,
  `from`, `to`, `end`, `default`, `interval`. Keep the Java/JSON name and map it with
  `@Column(name = "...")` to a safe column (e.g. field `year` → column `model_year`); for a table use
  `@Table(name = "app_user")` etc.
- Reference to another entity by id (not nested URL): `Long {other}Id` in request/response,
  `@ManyToOne(optional = false, fetch = FetchType.LAZY) @JoinColumn(name = "{other}_id")` in the
  entity, `BIGINT NOT NULL` + `CONSTRAINT fk_{table}_{other} FOREIGN KEY ({other}_id) REFERENCES {other} (id)`.
  The service loads the referenced entity and throws `NotFoundException` if missing.
  For URLs nested under a parent see [child-resource.md](child-resource.md).
# Backend templates

Placeholders: `{Entity}` (PascalCase), `{entity}` (camelCase), `{Entities}` / `{entities}` (plural),
`{package}`, `{table}`, `{url}` (e.g. `customers`), `{Key}` / `{key}` / `{key_column}` /
`{key label}` (the unique natural-key field, e.g. `Email` / `email` / `email` / `email`).
Lines marked `// each field` repeat per field from the field spec, in spec order.
Sections marked *(if unique)* exist only when the entity has a unique field; repeat them per unique field.

Package: `com.example.dealership.{package}`. All files in one package (main and test).

## Migrations

`backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/V{n}__{table}.sql`

```sql
CREATE TABLE {table} (
    id         BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    first_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,      -- each field, columns aligned
    nip        VARCHAR(10),
    CONSTRAINT uq_{table}_{key_column} UNIQUE ({key_column})
);
```

`V{n+1}__{table}_seed.sql`: 2–3 rows, every row valid against the Request validation and unique.

```sql
INSERT INTO {table} (first_name, nip) VALUES
    ('Jan', NULL),
    ('Anna', '5260250995');
```

## Entity

```java
package com.example.dealership.{package};

import jakarta.persistence.Column;
import jakarta.persistence.Entity;
import jakarta.persistence.GeneratedValue;
import jakarta.persistence.GenerationType;
import jakarta.persistence.Id;
import jakarta.persistence.Table;

@Entity
@Table(name = "{table}")
public class {Entity} {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    @Column(nullable = false, length = 100)   // each field: mirror the SQL column
    private String firstName;

    protected {Entity}() {
    }

    public {Entity}(String firstName /* , every field except id, spec order */) {
        this.firstName = firstName;
    }

    public Long getId() {
        return id;
    }

    // each field: getter + setter, no other methods
    public String getFirstName() {
        return firstName;
    }

    public void setFirstName(String firstName) {
        this.firstName = firstName;
    }
}
```

`java.time.LocalDate` / `java.math.BigDecimal` imports go first (java.*), then a blank line,
then `jakarta.*`, as in `Vehicle.java`. Enum columns: `@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)` above
`@Column(nullable = false, length = 20)`. Boolean: `@Column(nullable = false) private boolean x;`
with getter `isX()`.

## Enum

```java
package com.example.dealership.{package};

public enum {EnumName} {
    VALUE_ONE,
    VALUE_TWO
}
```

## Request / Response

```java
public record {Entity}Request(
        @NotBlank
        @Size(max = 100)
        String firstName,

        @Size(max = 10)
        @Pattern(regexp = "[0-9]{10}", message = "must be exactly 10 digits")
        String nip
) {
}
```

One annotation per line, a blank line between components (see `VehicleRequest`).

```java
public record {Entity}Response(
        Long id,
        String firstName,
        String nip
) {
}
```

## Mapper

```java
public final class {Entity}Mapper {

    private {Entity}Mapper() {
    }

    public static {Entity} toEntity({Entity}Request request) {
        return new {Entity}(
                request.firstName(),
                request.nip());
    }

    public static void updateEntity({Entity} {entity}, {Entity}Request request) {
        {entity}.setFirstName(request.firstName());
        {entity}.setNip(request.nip());
    }

    public static {Entity}Response toResponse({Entity} {entity}) {
        return new {Entity}Response(
                {entity}.getId(),
                {entity}.getFirstName(),
                {entity}.getNip());
    }
}
```

## Repository

```java
public interface {Entity}Repository extends JpaRepository<{Entity}, Long> {

    boolean existsBy{Key}(String {key});                 // (if unique) IgnoreCase variant for emails

    boolean existsBy{Key}AndIdNot(String {key}, Long id);
}
```

No unique field → empty interface body `{ }` on separate lines like a normal interface.

## Service

```java
@Service
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public class {Entity}Service {

    private final {Entity}Repository {entity}Repository;

    public {Entity}Service({Entity}Repository {entity}Repository) {
        this.{entity}Repository = {entity}Repository;
    }

    public List<{Entity}Response> findAll() {
        return {entity}Repository.findAll(Sort.by("id")).stream()
                .map({Entity}Mapper::toResponse)
                .toList();
    }

    public {Entity}Response findById(Long id) {
        return {Entity}Mapper.toResponse(get{Entity}(id));
    }

    @Transactional
    public {Entity}Response create({Entity}Request request) {
        if ({entity}Repository.existsBy{Key}(request.{key}())) {          // (if unique)
            throw {key}AlreadyExists(request.{key}());
        }
        {Entity} {entity} = {entity}Repository.save({Entity}Mapper.toEntity(request));
        return {Entity}Mapper.toResponse({entity});
    }

    @Transactional
    public {Entity}Response update(Long id, {Entity}Request request) {
        {Entity} {entity} = get{Entity}(id);
        if ({entity}Repository.existsBy{Key}AndIdNot(request.{key}(), id)) {   // (if unique)
            throw {key}AlreadyExists(request.{key}());
        }
        {Entity}Mapper.updateEntity({entity}, request);
        return {Entity}Mapper.toResponse({entity}Repository.save({entity}));
    }

    @Transactional
    public void delete(Long id) {
        {entity}Repository.delete(get{Entity}(id));
    }

    private {Entity} get{Entity}(Long id) {
        return {entity}Repository.findById(id)
                .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("{Entity} with id " + id + " not found"));
    }

    private static ConflictException {key}AlreadyExists(String {key}) {   // (if unique)
        return new ConflictException("{Entity} with {key label} " + {key} + " already exists");
    }
}
```

Optional unique field: guard with `request.{key}() != null && ...`.

## Controller

Identical to `VehicleController` with names replaced: `@RequestMapping("/api/{url}")`,
`findAll`, `findById`, `create` (201 + `ServletUriComponentsBuilder` Location), `update`,
`delete` (204). Constructor injection, `@Valid @RequestBody`.

## Test checklist

### `{Entity}ControllerTest` — `@WebMvcTest({Entity}Controller.class)`, `@MockitoBean {Entity}Service`

Constants: natural-key constant (e.g. `EMAIL`), `VALID_BODY` text block with every field (optional
ones filled), helpers `invalidBody()` and `response()`. Method names and assertions as in
`VehicleControllerTest`:

| Test | Asserts |
| --- | --- |
| `findAllReturns{Entities}` | 200, length 1, id, key field, one field of each kind (enum, date, boolean…) |
| `findByIdReturns{Entity}` | 200, key field |
| `findByIdReturnsNotFoundProblemWhen{Entity}DoesNotExist` | 404, `application/problem+json`, `status`, `detail` |
| `createReturnsCreated{Entity}` | 201, `Location` = `http://localhost/api/{url}/1`, id |
| `createReturnsBadRequestProblemWithFieldErrorsWhenRequestIsInvalid` | 400, `detail` = `Validation failed`, exact `errors.length()`, each `field` (sorted alphabetically) and at least one `message`; `verifyNoInteractions(service)` |
| `createReturnsEnglishValidationMessagesWhenAcceptLanguageIsPolish` | `Accept-Language: pl`, blank required field → `must not be blank` |
| `createReturnsBadRequestProblemWithFieldErrorWhen{EnumField}IsUnknown` *(per enum)* | `must be one of: A, B, C` |
| `createReturnsBadRequestProblemWithFieldErrorWhenValueHasWrongType` | number/date/boolean field given `"text"` (only strings? give a string field `{}`) → `has an invalid value` |
| `createReturnsBadRequestProblemWhenBodyIsNotJson` | `{ not json` → field `null`, `request body must be valid JSON` |
| `createReturnsConflictProblemWhen{Key}AlreadyExists` *(if unique)* | 409, detail from `ConflictException` |
| `createReturnsConflictProblemWhenDatabaseConstraintIsViolated` | `DataIntegrityViolationException("uq_{table}_{key_column}")` → 409 `Request conflicts with existing data` |
| `updateReturnsUpdated{Entity}` | 200 |
| `updateReturnsNotFoundProblemWhen{Entity}DoesNotExist` | 404 |
| `updateReturnsBadRequestProblemWithFieldErrorsWhenRequestIsInvalid` | 400 fields, no interactions |
| `updateReturnsConflictProblemWhen{Key}AlreadyExists` *(if unique)* | 409 |
| `deleteReturnsNoContent` | 204, `verify(service).delete(1L)` |
| `deleteReturnsNotFoundProblemWhen{Entity}DoesNotExist` | 404 via `doThrow` |

`invalidBody()`: break 3 fields of different kinds so that each produces **exactly one** error
(a blank required string without a pattern, a pattern/email violation, a range violation, a missing
required field). Errors are sorted by field name, then message — assert in that order.

### `{Entity}ServiceTest` — `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`, `@Mock` repository, `@InjectMocks` service

`findAllReturnsMapped{Entities}` (verifies `Sort.by("id")`), `findByIdThrowsNotFoundWhen{Entity}DoesNotExist`
(exact message), `createSaves{Entity}` (save answers its argument; assert mapped fields),
`createThrowsConflictWhen{Key}AlreadyExists` (exact message, `never()).save(any())`),
`updateChangesExisting{Entity}`, `updateThrowsConflictWhen{Key}BelongsToAnother{Entity}`,
`updateThrowsNotFoundWhen{Entity}DoesNotExist`, `deleteRemovesExisting{Entity}`,
`deleteThrowsNotFoundWhen{Entity}DoesNotExist`. Helpers `{entity}(key)` and `request(key)`,
constants `KEY` / `OTHER_KEY`. Optional unique field: add a test that `null` skips the check.
Custom business rules: one test per rule and per boundary.

### `{Entity}RepositoryTest` — `@DataJpaTest`, `TestEntityManager`

Use key values that differ from the seed data. `existsBy{Key}AndIdNotFinds{Key}OfAnother{Entity}`
(two saved rows, true/false/unknown key; for IgnoreCase also check different case) and
`saveStores{Entity}ThatCanBeReadBack` (flush, clear, `findById`, `isNotSameAs`, every field).
# Frontend templates

Placeholders as in [backend.md](backend.md), plus `{fe-file}` (singular kebab, e.g. `customer`),
`{fe-folder}` (plural kebab, e.g. `customers`), `{Label}` / `{Labels}` (UI text, e.g. `Customer`),
`{label}` (lowercase UI text). Folder: `frontend/src/app/{fe-folder}/`.
Start from a copy of the matching vehicle file and replace names and fields; the snippets below show
only what changes per entity.

## `{fe-file}-api.ts`

```ts
import { HttpClient, httpResource } from '@angular/common/http';
import { Injectable, Signal, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';

// per enum field:
export type CustomerType = 'PRIVATE' | 'COMPANY';
export const CUSTOMER_TYPE_LABELS: Record<CustomerType, string> = { PRIVATE: 'Private', COMPANY: 'Company' };
export const CUSTOMER_TYPES = Object.keys(CUSTOMER_TYPE_LABELS) as CustomerType[];

export interface {Entity} {
  id: number;
  firstName: string;        // each field, TS type from field-types.md, optional → `T | null`
  nip: string | null;
}

export type {Entity}Request = Omit<{Entity}, 'id'>;

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class {Entity}Api {
  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);
  private readonly url = '/api/{url}';
  // list(), get(id), create(), update(), delete(): identical to VehicleApi
}
```

## `{fe-folder}.routes.ts`

```ts
export const {entities}Routes: Routes = [
  { path: '', component: {Entity}List },
  { path: 'new', component: {Entity}Form },
  { path: ':id/edit', component: {Entity}Form },
  { path: ':id', component: {Entity}Detail },
];
```

`app.routes.ts`: add after the vehicles entry

```ts
  {
    path: '{fe-folder}',
    loadChildren: () => import('./{fe-folder}/{fe-folder}.routes').then((m) => m.{entities}Routes),
  },
```

`app.html`: add `<a routerLink="/{fe-folder}" routerLinkActive="active">{Labels}</a>` after the
existing links inside `<nav>`.

## List (`{fe-file}-list.ts/.html`)

Copy `vehicle-list`. Changes:
- `loadErrorMessage(error, '{Labels} not found')`.
- Heading `<h1>{Labels}</h1>`, link `Add {label}`.
- One `<th>` per displayed field (skip long text), last column `Actions`. First column is the key
  field (or the most identifying one) as a `routerLink` to the detail.
- Cell display per field-types.md (`?? '—'` for optional, labels for enums, `Yes/No` for booleans).
- `@empty` row: `colspan` = number of columns, text `No {labels} yet.`
- Expose label records used by the template as `protected readonly`.

## Detail (`{fe-file}-detail.ts/.html`)

Copy `vehicle-detail`. `<p><a routerLink="/{fe-folder}">Back to {labels}</a></p>`, `<h1>` with the
most human field(s) (e.g. `{{ customer.firstName }} {{ customer.lastName }}`), a `<dl>` with every
field (`<dt>` label, `<dd>` display), Edit link. Do not copy the vehicle "Documents" section.

## Form (`{fe-file}-form.ts/.html`)

`{Entity}FormModel` interface: strings as `string` (optional ones too), numbers `number | null`,
enums `Type | ''`, booleans `boolean`, dates `string`.

```ts
function toFormModel(customer: Customer | undefined): CustomerFormModel {
  return {
    firstName: customer?.firstName ?? '',
    nip: customer?.nip ?? '',
    active: customer?.active ?? false,
    rating: customer?.rating ?? null,
    type: customer?.type ?? '',
  };
}

function toRequest(model: CustomerFormModel): CustomerRequest {
  return {
    firstName: model.firstName,
    nip: model.nip || null,          // every optional string/date
    active: model.active,
    rating: model.rating!,           // required number
    type: model.type as CustomerType,
  };
}
```

Validators: one `required(path.x, { message: '{Field label} is required' })` per required field, in
field order. Nothing else. Submission/navigation/`problemDetailToFormErrors` identical to
`VehicleForm`, navigating to `['/{fe-folder}', saved.id]`. Not-found text `'{Entity} not found'`.

Template: copy `vehicle-form.html`; heading `Edit {label}` / `New {label}`; one block per field:

```html
    <label>
      First name
      <input type="text" [formField]="customerForm.firstName" />
    </label>
    @if (customerForm.firstName().touched()) {
      @for (error of customerForm.firstName().errors(); track error) {
        <p class="error" role="alert">{{ error.message }}</p>
      }
    }
```

Checkbox: `<label><input type="checkbox" [formField]="form.active" /> Active</label>`.
Select: as the fuel type select, with `<option value="">Select {field label lowercase}</option>`.
Cancel link: `isEdit() ? ['/{fe-folder}', id()] : ['/{fe-folder}']`.

## Form spec (`{fe-file}-form.spec.ts`)

Copy `vehicle-form.spec.ts` (same `beforeEach`, `afterEach(() => http.verify())`, helpers `fill`,
`select`, `submit`, `errors`). Inputs are found by `input[type="..."]` and index **in DOM order per
type** — recount after writing the template (`email`, `tel`, `date` are separate types from `text`).
Checkbox: `element.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[type="checkbox"]')[i].click()`.

`fillValid{Entity}()` fills only the required fields. Tests, all mandatory:

1. `shows required errors and sends nothing when the form is empty` — `http.expectNone('/api/{url}')`,
   exact list of required messages in field order.
2. `leaves format and range rules to the backend` — fill an invalid format value (e.g. email
   `not-an-email`), POST is sent with that value, flush a 400 with field errors, errors shown
   (displayed in DOM/field order, not response order).
3. `creates the {label} and navigates to its details` — fill all fields including optional ones,
   `expect(request.request.body).toEqual({...})` with **every** field, navigate to `['/{fe-folder}', 7]`.
   Add a variant assertion (or separate test) that empty optional fields are sent as `null`.
4. `loads the {label} in edit mode and updates it` — `setInput('id', '3')`, flush GET, change one field,
   PUT body `toEqual` the full entity without id.
5. `shows a dedicated message when the {label} to edit does not exist` — 404 → `'{Entity} not found'`.
6. `shows the ProblemDetail detail when loading the {label} fails` — 503 → detail text.
7. `shows object-level errors returned by the backend above the form` — 400 with `field: null`.
8. `shows field errors returned by the backend as ProblemDetail`.
9. `shows the ProblemDetail detail when the backend reports a conflict` — 409 with the real conflict
   message of the unique field (or a generic `Request conflicts with existing data` if none).
